.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt BENEXT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm benext
.Nd one-shot boot environment trials with fallback to a protected boot environment
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm protect Ar be
.Nm
.Cm try Ar be
.Nm
.Cm abort
.Nm
.Cm boot-arm
.Nm
.Cm confirm
.Nm
.Cm status Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm destroy Ar be
.Nm
.Cm rename Ar old new
.Nm
.Cm mount-rw Ar be dir
.Nm
.Cm prune Op Ar keep
.Nm
.Fl -check-config Op Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
boots a new boot environment once and falls back automatically.
The fallback order is: the one-shot trial, then the last good boot
environment, then the protected boot environment.
.Bl -tag -width "check-config"
.It Cm protect Ar be
Mark
.Ar be
as the protected boot environment
.Pq Va org.cloudbsd:protected=on .
Only one may be protected.
It cannot be destroyed, renamed, mounted read-write, tried, or pruned
through
.Nm .
.It Cm try Ar be
Record the current
.Va bootfs
as the last good boot environment, arm panic power-cycle in the running
system and in
.Ar be ,
and activate
.Ar be
for one boot with
.Nm bectl Cm activate Fl t .
Aborts if
.Va bootfs
changed.
.It Cm abort
Cancel a pending trial.
.It Cm boot-arm
Run early in boot by
.Pa rc.d/benext_arm .
Activates the protected boot environment for one boot, so a hard failure
of the current boot lands on it.
.It Cm confirm
Run late in boot by
.Pa rc.d/benext_confirm .
Runs the executable health checks in
.Va checks_dir .
On success, disarms and makes a trial permanent.
On failure, reboots to the fallback.
.It Cm status Op Fl -json
Print the state in human-readable form or JSON.
.It Cm prune Op Ar keep
Destroy old boot environments, keeping the original, active, next-boot,
last good, trial, and protected ones plus the newest
.Ar keep .
.It Fl -check-config Op Ar file
Validate the configuration; exit 0 if valid, 4 with a message if not.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /etc/benext/config.json
Configuration, see
.Xr benext.json 5 .
.It Pa /etc/benext.d/
Default health-check directory.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/benext_arm , Pa /etc/rc.d/benext_confirm
Boot hooks, enabled with
.Va benext_enable="YES"
in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for a bad argument or state, 3 when the protected boot
environment is refused, 4 for a configuration error, 5 when
.Va bootfs
changed during
.Cm try ,
64 for a usage error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr benext.json 5 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr bectl 8 ,
.Xr zfsbootcfg 8
.Sh BUGS
A hard failure of the last good boot environment before
.Pa rc.d/benext_arm
runs cannot reach the protected boot environment without loader support.
